23:player

276:Natsuki Shinomiya
277:I'm telling you, it's true... Why won't you believe me?!
279:Just last night, I saw green flames in the classroom!
280:Undoubtedly, a will-o'-the-wisp – a gathering of restless souls... No, that's not quite right. "Spectral fire"... yes, that's a better term for it.
282:Is there even a difference?
284:Green flames... It's certainly a bit strange, isn't it?
285:Mirai
286:Just calm down a little bit. Where exactly did you see it? Don't tell me it was in the lab building...
287:Green flames... That's probably copper burning.
288:Yui Yagi
289:Flame test.
290:A familiar voice comes from behind. I turn around, and, as expected, it's Yui Yagi.
291:Come to think of it, she seldom talks outside of mahjong and seems somewhat nervous now.
292:Ah – ahh! So it's just a flame test thing!
293:That's the one! It's discovered by that famous professor... What's his name again?
294:Isn't the flame test from junior high textbooks?
295:Oh... Is... is that so?
296:Electrons in metals absorb energy when heated, and jump to unstable higher energy levels.
297:After that, they spontaneously fall back to lower energy levels, releasing photons of different energies...
298:Right – those photons correspond to wavelengths of light, which is why the flame changes color!
299:That's our Yui! Spot-on, just like usual.
300:Wait... was this also covered in junior high?
301:...Nah, no way they taught the actual theory in junior high.
302:As we keep joking around, Yui and Mirai suddenly click – their scientific discussion grows more intense and technical by the second.
303:Professional terms we'd never even heard before come flying out one after another, leaving absolutely no room for the rest of us to get a word in.
304:At this rate, Natsuki and I are about to fade into the background like NPCs... What should we do?
305:Hey, since there are four of us now... wanna go play some mahjong?
306:Mahjong? I'd love to... but not today.
307:I've got an invention symposium I have to attend – oh shoot, it's almost time! Gotta go now!
308:Ah, I should probably head out too – got my shift at the bar starting soon. Sorry, guys!
309:Oh... what a shame. Guess we'll have to wait for next time, then...
310:Uh... so...
311:And just like that, only Yui and I stay.
312:...
313:So... We...?
314:How about we just call it here?
315:Under the weight of that awkward silence, Yui doesn't say a word. She just looks at me.
316:Her expression remains as unreadable as ever – those eyes give away nothing.
317:Does she not want to leave yet? Guess it's up to me to break the ice...
319:It seems that you are really into science.
321:Is there something on my face?
322:...Not really sure about that.
323:Huh? What does that mean?
324:Since my parents are scientists, I've been reading science books since I was little.
326:But... you know so much about everything...
327:That's why I thought you were into science.
328:...Is that so?
329:...If you say it like that, then I guess maybe I do.
330:If you don't want to be a scientist... then what do you want to be?
331:Well...?
332:...Right. What do I want to do?
333:...
334:...What kind of person do I truly want to become...?
335:Eh? Is that too deep...? Sorry! You don't really need to take it that seriously!
336:I just wanted to make some small talk...
337:But Yui turned serious... She seems genuinely troubled by my words.
338:Not good – better change the subject fast...
340:Science aside, there are plenty of other things we can talk about.
341:...Mhm. Thank you, senpai.
342:Yui remains silent, her gaze still locked onto me.
343:Wait... could my offhand remark actually be right? Gotta wipe my face just to check.
344:...You guessed right, senpai.
345:Eh? Is there really something on my face?
346:Yes, it's the look on your face... quite amusing to observe.
347:If you don't like me doing that, I'll stop. Sorry.
349:It's... not that I don't like it...
351:Eh... You find observing me that interesting?
352:After all, by every possible measure, I'm just... thoroughly average in One Han City.
353:...Your reactions are kind of fascinating.
354:Senpai, you really should be more aware of your own interesting side.
355:Wait... are you teasing me?
356:I'm telling the truth.
357:Is... that so...
358:Usually, someone with Yui's personality should be the more interesting one...
359:We should be heading the same way home, right?
360:I've seen you at the convenience store near my place before. So I figured we must live close by.
361:Really? I didn't even notice...
362:But even if we're not, I'd be happy to walk you home today.
363:Mmhm.
365:Do you usually cook at home, Yui?
366:Yeah. Still practicing, though.
367:Then let's hit the supermarket on the way. I need to grab a few things too.
368:Afterward, we head to the supermarket nearby.
369:It's a well-stocked supermarket, so we should be able to find everything we need.
370:Mm... I'm out of milk too. Might as well grab some while we're here.
371:What are you planning to make tonight, Yui?
372:Wait, don't tell me. Let me take a guess.
373:The ingredients in her shopping basket should give away what she's planning to make.
374:Let me see... Lettuce, kale, romaine, red leaf lettuce...?
375:Green cabbage, red cabbage, savoy cabbage...
376:Mm... Yui...
377:Seriously, what are you gonna do with all these leafy greens?
378:Didn't you just say you're gonna take a guess?
380:Could it be... some kind of hodgepodge!
382:Is it that you have a pet rabbit?
383:Wrong answer.
384:Is it that hard to guess?
385:Well... pretty hard.
386:So... what's the answer?
387:Beef and potato stew.
388:Huh?
389:Then... what about the potatoes?
390:Technically, you don't have to put potatoes in beef and potato stew.
391:Only by daring to try new ingredients can we forge new paths in cuisine... Probably.
392:But... if you don't add potatoes, it's not even beef and potato stew anymore...
393:Why do I feel like that she's innovating in the wrong direction...
394:Wait... does this mean you can't actually cook...?
395:...See? You really are interesting.
396:Though I've never had a pet.
397:Is that so... I saw your basket was full of veggies, so I thought...
398:The correct answer is beef and potato stew.
399:Also, feeding rabbits too many veggies can be dangerous.
400:Veggies are mainly for hydration, so you should only give them a tiny amount. 3 grams per kilogram of their weight is the absolute maximum.
401:Hold up! Don't think I didn't hear that terrifying "correct" answer just now!
402:Actually, for rabbits, hay is far more nutritious than fresh vegetables.
403:Senpai, don't you find it amazing?
404:Uh... you're derailing the conversation hard.
405:How are you gonna make beef and potato stew with these?
406:You have to dare to break the old rules sometimes.
407:Look, potatoes in beef and potato stew isn't a "rule" – it's literally in the name!
408:???
409:Waaah...
410:A child's crying echoes from nearby.
411:Looking around, a little girl – about four or five years old – stands in front of the bakery display, looking utterly lost.
412:...Could she have gotten separated from her family?
413:Since it's a weekday afternoon, there are barely any customers in the supermarket, and no staff nearby either.
414:(Well... Should we go help?)
415:...Let's go check on her.
416:Yui strides ahead of me, swiftly walking over to the little girl.
417:She crouches down to meet the little girl eye to eye, her voice softening as she gently asks what's wrong.
418:What happened to you?
419:Did you get separated from your mommy and daddy?
420:Little Girl
421:...Sniffle.
422:Mommy... Where's Mommy...?
423:It's okay.
424:We'll help you find her.
425:There's no customer service desk on this floor...
426:Senpai, you'll help too, right?
427:Sure, we'll help you find your mommy together.
428:Thank you...
429:So, do you remember where you last saw her?
430:I was looking at the bubble guns earlier...
431:I kept looking... and then Mommy was gone.
433:So... what's the best way to handle this?
435:Let's go check the second floor.
437:Let's wait near the exit.
439:This should be where she got separated from her mom.
440:We've searched around the toy shelves but haven't seen anyone who looks like her mother...
441:If her mom's also looking for her, she might have already gone somewhere else, right?
442:Mommy...
443:Where did Mommy go...?
444:Tears well up in the little girl's eyes again... This is bad. We're completely clueless about what to do.
445:Perhaps it would be better to ask a staff member to help?
446:At the very least, we should be able to use the store's PA system – it's better than nothing...
447:Don't worry, we'll find her for sure.
448:Unlike my panicked self, Yui remains as calmly composed as ever. And for some reason, there's an unusual gentleness about her now.
449:She crouches beside the little girl again, gently stroking her hair.
450:Do you know why soapy water can blow perfectly round bubbles?
451:And why plain water can't do the same?
452:Sniff... sniffle...
453:Sniffle... I don't know...
454:...How did we get onto blowing bubbles?
455:Imagine that we have a cup filled with water.
456:The water in the cup is actually made up of countless tiny particles.
457:We call them "molecules."
458:What... what does that mean...
459:...Sorry. Let me put it in simpler terms.
460:Alright...
461:...Little fairies.
462:There are many, many little fairies living in the water in the cup.
463:Of course, it's just a metaphor. Little fairies aren't real – it's just to simplify the explanation.
464:That's right, Yui! The fairies explanation is perfect!
465:No need to explain that part...
466:...I see.
467:Little fairies? ...Are they even smaller than me?
468:Yes, they're so tiny that we can't even see them.
469:But you know – those little fairies work really hard.
470:They hold each other's hands so hard, trying to keep the water from scattering into a puddle.
471:And so, they form a sphere, because that's the most stable shape.
472:Now we need to talk about the concept of surface tension, because surfactants weaken the cohesion between water molecules...
473:Yui, you're going too far again!
474:This is so tough...
475:The little girl probably doesn't understand a single word of Yui's explanation.
476:Yet somehow, her tears have stopped, replaced now by a soft smile.
477:Perhaps it's the focus in Yui's explanation that is drawing her in.
478:Also... maybe it's just my imagination, but now her eyes are glowing with pure curiosity.
479:I get it now!
480:The soap bubbles are round because the fairies are holding hands!
481:That's right...!
482:Yui clears her throat, then gently pats the girl's head.
483:So, until we find your mom... let's hold our hands, okay?
484:As long as we work together like the little fairies in the water, we'll definitely find her!
485:Although Yui seems a little embarrassed saying this, I think it's remarkable that she managed to say it out loud.
486:I thought she wasn't great with people... but maybe I just didn't know her well enough.
487:Yui takes the little girl's hand and walks ahead of me. Watching their backs, I feel a sudden warmth in my chest.
488:...Ellie? Is that you?
489:An anxious voice calls out from behind us.
490:We turn around and see a long-haired woman standing at the escalator landing.
491:The little girl dashes toward her with pure joy – finally, a mother-daughter reunion.
492:Little Girl's Mother
493:Thank you so much, both of you! Ellie, come say thank you too!
494:Thank you for helping me find Mommy!
495:Don't get lost again, okay? Be careful next time.
496:Okay! I will!
497:Yui waves goodbye to the mother and daughter, and the corners of her eyes seem to crinkle, just a little...
498:Is she... smiling?
499:Now that I think about it... even though her facial muscles barely move, if you look closely, her emotions show through.
500:...This is quite the discovery.
501:...I'm so glad we found her.
502:Yeah, and it's all thanks to you.
503:It's because you treated that little girl with kindness that she was willing to come with us.
504:I only did that... for myself.
505:Looking at that little girl, it was like seeing my past self.
506:Your past self?
507:...Oh.
508:Hm? What is it?
509:I forgot there's a delivery coming today.
510:Eh? When would that be?
511:Between 4 and 6 PM. It should be arriving any minute now.
512:I check my phone. It's 20 minutes left until 5 PM.
513:Uh... what do we do? Can you still make it?
514:Sorry, senpai. I have to head back home now.
515:Sure, be safe on your way!
516:You too.
517:Yui has just sprinted a few meters when she suddenly stops and turns back.
518:At this moment, her expression is still a bit hard for me to read.
519:It's been a fun day.
520:See you at the mahjong table, senpai.
521:The way she's standing... It's like she's reluctant to leave.
522:Hope it's not just me overthinking.
523:Rather than searching aimlessly, why don't we wait at a spot where her mother is sure to pass by?
524:Brilliant strategy...!
525:Although it's a bit exaggerated, being praised by Yui feels pretty good.
526:Once the little girl calms down, we guide her toward the supermarket exit.
527:As I expected, the little girl's mother appears before us shortly after.
528:Mommy! Where have you been?!
529:Ellie suddenly disappeared, so Mommy was looking for you...
530:Ah, are we having curry tonight?
531:Eh? I guess we are?
532:That's just how kids are, switching topics so fast that even her mom can't keep up... Before leaving, the little girl's mother gave us her sincere thanks.
533:After waving goodbye to the little girl, Yui murmurs something beside me.
534:I'm thinking about curry too.
535:Now that you mention it...
536:But the ingredients you bought won't work for curry, right? Should we head back to the fresh produce section?
537:Hm? Didn't we already buy all the ingredients?
538:It's common knowledge that beef stew with potatoes and curry basically use the same ingredients.
539:...I don't even know where to begin...
540:Regardless, Yui seems determined to make curry tonight, so we head to the spice aisle.
541:Uh, Yui, you're not thinking of making the spices yourself, are you?
542:Maybe we should try store-bought curry powder or roux first...?
543:Wait, you really don't need chili bean sauce in curry! Just put that down first!
544:...So I only add it after mastering curry techniques?
545:Not really... How should I put it, at least the concept of curry doesn't include...
546:Oh right. Senpai, next time we play mahjong, I'll bring you my homemade curry.
547:Ah, hmm... I'll look forward to it.
548:Yui's face remains expressionless – but as she meticulously selects spices, I can almost sense a hint of joy.
549:...But when I think about what comes next...
550:I can't really say I'm feeling joyful as well...
551:Did you say something?
552:N-no, nothing!
557:Our Ordinary Days
558:Activity Room, National University of Fuuchi
561:Well, that's something you can figure out later, one step at a time.
562:Ah, I just remembered, my fridge is empty...
563:Bubble guns... should be in the toy aisle. Is it on the second floor?
564:We take the little girl to the second floor.
565:However... I don't actually want to become a scientist myself. I'm probably different from those who genuinely love science.
